From: Janine Tombs <janine.tombs@gama-aviation.example> (Gama Aviation FZC)
To: Khalaf Ahmed Al Otaiba <chairman@bin-otaiba.example> (Bin Otaiba Investment Group)
Date: 2023-03-23
Subject: RE: Aircraft Global 5000 - amounts due to 31 December 2022

Dear Sir,

We acknowledge your offer of 6 February 2023 to pay US$711,408.25 for the items stated. Our position on the amounts due is:
i) the stated items, correctly calculated, come to US$200,758.14 more than your figure;
ii) maintenance: the full amount due is set out in Appendix 1, totalling US$961,255.85. A plan for the return to service of the aircraft will only be produced once the amounts due are paid in full; meanwhile we will perform only those tasks necessary to preserve its condition;
iii) parking/hangarage: discounted by a third but due and payable, US$395,958.00;
iv) contractual interest on late payments: US$236,845.46.

The total, US$2,506,225.70, is the amount due and payable under the AMA up to 31 December 2022. Please pay that sum by 31 March 2023.

Yours faithfully,
Janine Tombs
Managing Director, Gama Aviation FZC

